  "style": {
    "name": "Lapis Meridian (jubilant Mughal)",
    "rationale": "Second pass: kept all four chattris and corner pinnacles ENGAGED to the parapet (no detached kiosks), deepened the central iwan into a ~6-block gold-framed pishtaq recess over a dark prismarine threshold, articulated both flanks into pilastered two-bay grids of recessed lapis-and-jade pietra-dura panels so no wall field exceeds ~5 blocks, banded the plinth and cornice with jade and gold string-courses, and rebuilt the gold onion dome with a belly (y39-40, width 13) that overhangs its drum (width 9) so it reads as a dome not a pyramid — holding the amber-vs-azure complementary palette and refusing the reference's white."
